Rules are confirmed on real labels: [0.969, 1.0, 0.953, 1.0]. Skills 0 and 2 miss 3-5%, which is one or two wrong code entries (about 3.1% each) or label noise. I rank doubtful entries by evidence over recent checkpoints and try the top alternative in each, since a true fix should add about 3.1% and breaking a correct entry should lose about 3.1%.
```python
